cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the underlying physics papers listed in the README."
title: "TFQKD_MultiTurbulence: Twin-Field QKD over free-space channels with multiple turbulence models"
version: 2.4.0
license: MIT
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kumar"
    given-names: "Anand"
    affiliation: "Centre for Applied Research in Electronics (CARE), Indian Institute of Technology Delhi, New Delhi, India"
abstract: >-
  Python framework for twin-field quantum key distribution over free-space optical links, with
  Log-Normal, Gamma-Gamma, corrected Gamma-Gamma and beam-broadening turbulence models applied
  independently on each arm. Developed by Anand Kumar during a research internship at CARE, IIT Delhi (June to December 2026), under the supervision of Dr. Neelkanth Kundu,
  with Dr. Ramniwas Meena as co-supervisor. Supported by the National Quantum Mission (NQM) and the
  Samngya Foundation.
keywords:
  - quantum key distribution
  - twin-field QKD
  - free-space optics
  - atmospheric turbulence
  - Gamma-Gamma
